      "Title": "Synopsis",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for unrtf is now available for openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4",
      "Title": "Summary",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "UnRTF is a command-line program written in C which converts documents in Rich Text Format (.rtf) to HTML, LaTeX, troff macros, and RTF itself. Converting to HTML, it supports a number of features of Rich Text Format:     * Changes in the text\u0026apos;s font, size, weight (bold), and slant (italic)     * Underlines and strikethroughs     * Partial support for text shadowing, outlining, embossing, or engraving     * Capitalizations     * Superscripts and subscripts     * Expanded and condensed text     * Changes in the foreground and background colors     * Conversion of special characters to HTML entities\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nUnRTF by GNU Project is vulnerable to out-of-bounds write. If a user opens an RTF file crafted by an attacker, it may lead to a denial-of-service (DoS) condition.(CVE-2026-109831)",
      "Title": "Description",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for unrtf is now available for openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4.\n\nopenEuler Security has rated this update as having a security impact of medium. A Common Vunlnerability Scoring System(CVSS)base score,which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVElink(s) in the References section.",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "Medium",
      "Title": "Severity",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "unrtf",
      "Title": "Affected Component",
      "Type": "General"
    }
  ],
